  data: {
    LLM: "ROUND STRUCTURE:\n- Round = 1-3 successive deals by same dealer (maki-yaku)\n- Round ends when kankei loses a deal or wins 3 successive deals\n- New dealer is player to right of previous dealer FIRST DEAL OF ROUND:\n1. Trump suit determined by round number (clubs, diamonds, hearts rotating; spades for final round 'Tome-Suppe')\n2. Dealer deals 10 cards each\n3. Joker holder and trump ace holder declare 'kan' and become partners (kankei)\n4. If same player holds both, they partner with player two places to their right\n5. Partners must not sit adjacent; exchange seats if necessary\n6. Partners exchange information by showing cards PLAY:\n1. Kankei decides who leads first ('Iku' = I lead, 'Koi' = You lead)\n2. Must follow suit if possible; joker can be played to any trick (except first and last)\n3. Joker always wins trick; if no joker, highest trump wins; if no trump, highest of led suit wins\n4. Joker holder cannot be forced to play joker until 9th trick (odori ban)",
    Player: "ROUND STRUCTURE:\n- Round = 1-3 successive deals by same dealer (maki-yaku)\n- Round ends when kankei loses a deal or wins 3 successive deals\n- New dealer is player to right of previous dealer FIRST DEAL OF ROUND:\n1. Trump suit determined by round number (clubs, diamonds, hearts rotating; spades for final round 'Tome-Suppe')\n2. Dealer deals 10 cards each\n3. Joker holder and trump ace holder declare 'kan' and become partners (kankei)\n4. If same player holds both, they partner with player two places to their right\n5. Partners must not sit adjacent; exchange seats if necessary\n6. Partners exchange information by showing cards PLAY:\n1. Kankei decides who leads first ('Iku' = I lead, 'Koi' = You lead)\n2. Must follow suit if possible; joker can be played to any trick (except first and last)\n3. Joker always wins trick; if no joker, highest trump wins; if no trump, highest of led suit wins\n4. Joker holder cannot be forced to play joker until 9th trick (odori ban)",
    objective: 'The kankei (partnership of joker holder and trump ace holder) tries to win more than 8 of the 16 available points (ace, king, queen, jack of each suit). The mukankei (other players) try to prevent this.',
